    "text": "By Kelvine ,\n8 hours ago There is a particular kind of insect that becomes much easier to notice around North Carolina homes when the air finally starts losing its summer warmth. It may be sitting flat against a bedroom window, crawling slowly across siding, or resting near a porch light, with a long brown body and strange flattened shapes on its back legs that make it look almost unfamiliar. Read full article",
